  "title": "LOG10 executes x87 FLDLG2 + FYL2X directly, differing from LOG(x, 10)",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20430, LOG10(x) rejects x <= 0 with #NUM! and executes the x87 FLDLG2 + FYL2X fused logarithm stored to binary64. Unlike LOG(x, 10) (which divides two x87 LN calls), LOG10 returns exact 3 on 1000 and -1 on 0.1, and differs by 1 ULP on general inputs such as 8.501181837508149e-308 (LOG10 gives 0xc0733120da4ebbc1 vs LOG(x, 10) = 0xc0733120da4ebbc0). All 2,823 full-bank LOG10 rows match.",
